course: dictionary
lesson: 15231
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and shaker is one of them. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning to use. «Mum put the pepper shaker back on the table.» Here a shaker is a small container with holes in the lid, used for shaking out pepper.
explain: «The music teacher gave us egg shakers to keep the beat.» Egg shakers rattle when you shake them, so here a shaker is a musical instrument. Music, beat and rattle are the clues. The same word can name a different thing.
explain: Some meanings are special. A Shaker, with a capital S, is a member of a small Christian group in the USA. In «movers and shakers», shakers means important people who make things happen. Ask yourself: is this about food, music, a drink, or people?
fact: A shaker is a noun, so it names a thing or a person. The plural is shakers.
fact: A salt shaker or pepper shaker is a container with small holes in the lid, for shaking out powder.
fact: A shaker can also be a container you shake to mix drinks, such as a protein shaker or milkshake shaker.
fact: An egg shaker or maraca is a musical instrument filled with beads or seeds that rattles when shaken.
fact: A Shaker with a capital letter is a member of a small Christian group in the USA, known for simple, handmade furniture.
exercise: «Dad poured the sugar from the shaker onto his porridge.» What is a shaker here? | A member of a religious group | *A container with holes in the lid for shaking out sugar | A tall glass for milk | A musical instrument
exercise: «We kept the beat with egg shakers in music.» What kind of shaker is this? | A salt container | *A musical instrument that rattles | A member of a religious group | A drink mixer
exercise: In «movers and shakers», what do shakers mean? | Musical instruments | Containers for drinks | Members of a religious group | *Important people who make things happen
test: «Ella mixed her protein powder in a shaker after football.» What is the shaker? | A musical instrument | *A container you shake to mix a drink | A Shaker from the USA | A salt container
test: Which meaning fits Shaker with a capital S? | *A member of a small Christian group in the USA | A powder container for the table | An important person | A rattling instrument full of beads
exam: Which meaning of shaker fits «The Shakers made simple, careful furniture by hand»? | *A member of a religious group, the Shakers | A kitchen container | A drink mixer | A musical instrument
